          "name": "Freefall",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "A flying or jumping opinicus can land on foes as a standard action, using its whole body to crush them. This is treated as a crush attack, except the opinicus can use it against opponents two or more size categories smaller than itself. A crush attack affects as many creatures as fit in the opinicus's space. Creatures in the affected area must succeed on a Reflex save (DC 24) or be pinned, automatically taking bludgeoning damage during the next round unless the opinicus moves off them. If the opinicus chooses to maintain the pin, it must succeed at a combat maneuver check as normal. Pinned foes take damage from the crush each round if they don't escape.",
